import java.util.*;

public class CommentUtil {
    public static Map<String, List<String>> getAllComments(Map<String, @UnmodifiableView List<String>> allComments) {
        return Collections.unmodifiableMap(allComments);
    }

    public static void printCommentInfo(String commentId, String username, int commentsCount) {
        System.out.println("Comment ID: " + commentId);
        System.out.println("Username: " + username);
        System.out.println("Number of Comments: " + commentsCount);
    }
}
```

And here's an example usage:

```java
import java.util.*;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        // Create a map to store comments
        Map<String, @UnmodifiableView List<String>> allComments = new HashMap<>();
        
        // Add some sample comments
        allComments.put("comment1", Arrays.asList("Username1", "Comment 1"));
        allComments.put("comment2", Arrays.asList("Username2", "Comment 2"));

        // Get all comments
        Map<String, List<String>> getAllComments = CommentUtil.getAllComments(allComments);

        // Print comment info
        CommentUtil.printCommentInfo("comment1", "Username1", 2);
        CommentUtil.printCommentInfo("comment2", "Username2", 3);
    }
}
```

This `CommentUtil` class provides two methods: `getAllComments` to retrieve all comments and `printCommentInfo` to print comment information. The `getAllComments` method returns an unmodifiable map of comments, and the `printCommentInfo` method prints the ID, username, and number of comments for a given comment.
